{"generated":"2026-08-03T12:26:00.261336+00:00","period_start":"2026-07-27T15:07:00+00:00","period_end":"2026-08-03T11:51:00+00:00","snapshot_count":41,"html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>The Vendetta Gazette — August 10, 2026</title>\n<style>\n  body { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: #f5ecd7; color: #1a1a1a; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }\n  h1 { text-align: center; font-size: 2.8em; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; border-top: 6px double #1a1a1a; border-bottom: 6px double #1a1a1a; padding: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 4px; }\n  h2 { text-align: center; font-size: 1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\n  h3 { font-size: 1.35em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a1a; margin-top: 24px; }\n  p { line-height: 1.75; margin: 10px 0; text-align: justify; }\n  blockquote { background: #e8d9b5; border: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 20px 0; padding: 16px 20px; font-style: italic; }\n  blockquote strong { display: block; font-style: normal; font-size: 1.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding-bottom: 4px; }\n  hr { border: none; border-top: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 28px 0; }\n  .subhead { font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05em; display: block; margin-top: -6px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: #444; }\n  .byline { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block; }\n  .leaderboard { background: #1a1a1a; color: #f5ecd7; padding: 12px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }\n  .leaderboard strong { display: block; text-align: center; font-size: 1.1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f5ecd7; padding-bottom: 4px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>The Vendetta Gazette</h1>\n<h2>Vol. XVIII &bull; August 10, 2026 &bull; &ldquo;All the Blood That&rsquo;s Fit to Print&rdquo; &bull; Two Cents (If You&rsquo;re Still Alive to Pay)</h2>\n\n<div class=\"leaderboard\">\n  <strong>&#9733; TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK &#9733;</strong>\n  Wu-Tang &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +151 turfs<br>\n  Claude &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +138 turfs<br>\n  Flattop &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +93 turfs<br>\n  Free Willy &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +5 turfs<br>\n  Donald Trump &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +1 turf\n</div>\n\n<h3>Wu-Tang Dethrones Claude — By A Whisker, By a War, and By Sheer Magnificent Savagery</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">The Iron Fist of the East Side Seizes One Hundred and Fifty-One Turfs, Displacing Last Fortnight's Champion — Though Both Men Lay Waste to the Empire of the Fallen Fifth Blood Emperor</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>Dear readers, last week your correspondent rashly declared that Claude — that relentless, methodical, utterly inexorable conqueror — had rendered all competition academic. This week, Vendetta City itself has seen fit to correct the record, and it has done so in the most spectacular fashion imaginable: by producing a challenger whose territorial appetite makes even Claude look, for one extraordinary seven-day span, merely <em>mortal</em>.</p>\n\n<p>Wu-Tang, known in certain East Side gambling dens as &ldquo;the Iron Fist&rdquo; and in less charitable establishments as &ldquo;the fellow who took everything you owned and smiled while doing it,&rdquo; has claimed <strong>one hundred and fifty-one turfs</strong> this week — the single greatest territorial haul this gazette has recorded since we began keeping score. Claude, no slouch himself with a formidable one hundred and thirty-eight new blocks added to his already vast dominion, must for once content himself with second billing. The city holds its breath. The rivalry, gentlemen, is <em>on.</em></p>\n\n<p>But to understand how these two titans feasted so extravagantly, one must examine the carcass upon which they dined. The outfit known as <strong>FIFTH BLOOD EMPEROR</strong> — once a name that commanded whispered respect in the back booths of a dozen speakeasies — has suffered a catastrophe of Napoleonic proportions. No fewer than <strong>one hundred and thirty-seven</strong> of his territories were seized this week, the vast bulk of them swallowed whole by Wu-Tang's relentless eastern advance, with Claude picking clean whatever scraps remained. Five hundred of the Emperor's garrison troops have likewise vanished — captured, dispersed, or simply fled the advancing columns. The Emperor's empire has not merely contracted; it has <em>collapsed</em>. Whether the man himself has gone to ground, gone to the law, or simply gone, this reporter cannot confirm. His silence, however, speaks volumes.</p>\n\n<p>Wu-Tang's campaign was prosecuted with a ferocity that left veteran street observers genuinely agape. One hundred and thirty-eight territorial captures in a single week, supported by precision strikes on two rival headquarters — all while absorbing the inevitable cost of such aggression: five hundred and thirty-eight garrison units shed in the fighting, his armies now standing at three thousand six hundred and twenty-four. Make no mistake — that is not weakness. That is the price of conquest, paid willingly by a man who clearly considers it a bargain.</p>\n\n<p>Claude, meanwhile, demonstrated that last week's sixty-one-turf performance was no ceiling but merely a warm-up. One hundred and thirty-eight new turfs, eleven enemy headquarters stormed and seized, thirty-three brazen cash raids netting a tidy share of the week's total plunder of nineteen thousand dollars and change — all while adding one hundred and thirty-three fresh troops to his garrison. Claude does not merely expand. Claude <em>compounds.</em></p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"192\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wu-Tang</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+151</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Claude</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"365\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"531\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+138</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Flattop</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"246\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"412\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+93</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"179\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+5</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"2\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"168\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+1</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<h3>Flattop Finds His Ferocity — Thirteen Headquarters Taken in Seven Days</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">The City's Most Prolific HQ-Breaker This Week Was Not Wu-Tang, Nor Claude — It Was the Man They Keep Underestimating</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>While the headlines naturally belong to the titans of territorial expansion, a sharp-eyed reader will note that the week's most decorated headquarters-wrecker was, improbably, <strong>Flattop</strong>. Thirteen enemy headquarters breached and captured in a single week — a number that would be the undisputed story of any ordinary edition of this gazette, and which is here reduced to a secondary column purely by the freakish scale of events elsewhere\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HEAVIEST LOSSES THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">FIFTH BLOOD EMPEROR</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-134</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Vitolio</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"23\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"189\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-8</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">ZERO</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"11\